\title{Detecting simplicial continuity}
\meta{source}{[[MR23]]}
\import{common}

\p{First, let us consider the general situation of detecting continuity. We assume we're working in a spatial/local type theory with modalities #{\flat \dashv \sharp} where #{\sharp} is a reflection and #{\flat} a coreflection. In the simplicial case #{\flat} will be #{\skeleton_0} and #{\sharp} will be #{\coskeleton_0}.}

\transclude{fb-0045}
\transclude{fb-0046}

\p{The following is Theorem 3.1.6 of [[MR23]]:}
\transclude{fb-0048}

\p{Indeed, they argue semantically in Remark 3.1.4 of [[MR23]] that any family #{G_i} that generates a local topos \topos{E} under colimits will detect continuity for the focus given by the terminal map of toposes #{\Gamma \colon \topos{E} \to \Space}.}


\p{In [[MR23]] they propose the following axiom for simplicial type theory:}

\transclude{fb-0049}

\p{Unfolding what this axiom means in the context of [the previous theorem](fb-0048), a crisp map #{{f \colon-flat X \to Y}} is an [[hott-000U]] if #{f_n \colon X_n \to Y_n} is an equivalence for all #{n :^\flat \bN}, where ##{X_n \defeq \skeleton_0(\Delta^n \to X)\mathrlap{.}}}
